WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.910
Two thermometers stand side by side.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:05.160
One reads in degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.840
The other reads in degrees Fahrenheit.

4
00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:12.130
When the Celsius one shows one hundred,
the Fahrenheit one shows two hundred and

5
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.310
twelve.

6
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:15.410
Now cool them down together.

7
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:19.320
At nought Celsius, the
Fahrenheit one shows thirty-two.

8
00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.880
The gap is shrinking.

9
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.200
Keep cooling.

10
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.170
Will the two readings ever match?

11
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.070
Or is Fahrenheit always the bigger number?

12
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:32.800
In this mission, you'll use the formula F
equals one point eight C plus thirty-two.

13
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.720
You'll substitute negative numbers,
putting them in brackets so the signs come

14
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:37.680
out right.

15
00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:42.650
And you'll rearrange a formula, undoing
each operation in reverse order.

16
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.390
Your mission: find out if one temperature
reads the same on both scales.
